[#- The rules of Renovate for what the osv-scanner.toml of the project accepts, as
    blueprint.py advisories writes them: none in a new repository of any kind, since
    the blueprint accepts no version of the test tools of Home Assistant in
    stacks/home-assistant/ either. Once it accepts one there again, an integration
    takes the blueprint's own .github/renovate-accepted.json5, whose lock file it has
    in its root: the macro of includes/replace.jinja with "stacks/home-assistant/"
    replaced by nothing, for the stack home-assistant, which stops the render while
    the file names no such path. test_renovate_tries_no_fix_of_what_osv_scanner_accepts
    fails until it does. -#]
